          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "مزرعه (mazra'e) — \"a farm; a field (of crops)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "پدربزرگم یک مزرعه کوچک در روستا دارد. Pedarbozorgam yek mazra'e-ye kuchek dar rustâ dârad. My grandfather has a small farm in the village."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Arabic plural mazâre'."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "mazra'e was borrowed from Arabic mazraʿa (EtymDB), a place where seed is sown."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
