          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "شالیزار (shâlizâr) — \"a rice paddy, a paddy field\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "در شمال شالیزارهای سبز زیادی هست. Dar shomâl shâlizâr-hâ-ye sabz-e ziyâdi hast. In the north there are many green rice paddies."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "shâli 'rice in the husk' + -zâr 'a place full of'."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "shâlizâr is built from shâli 'rice in the husk' and the native ending -zâr 'a place full of', as in golzâr 'a rose garden'. The origin of shâli is not settled, and EtymDB does not list it."
            }
          ]
        },
